From: meta-xuantie <noreply@xuantie.invalid>
Date: Wed, 29 Jul 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] pkg_resources: guard pkgutil.ImpImporter for Python 3.13

setuptools 65.0.2 targets CPython <= 3.11. pkg_resources registers finders
and namespace handlers keyed on pkgutil.ImpImporter, which was deprecated in
3.3 and REMOVED in 3.12. Because both registrations run at module import
time, merely importing pkg_resources (and thus setuptools) aborts with
"AttributeError: module 'pkgutil' has no attribute 'ImpImporter'" on the
python 3.13 backport, breaking every native recipe that uses setuptools
(meson-native, glib-2.0-native, btrfs-tools, ...).

Guard both registrations behind hasattr(pkgutil, 'ImpImporter'). The
FileFinder registrations immediately below already cover the real import
system on 3.3+, so the ImpImporter path is pure legacy and safe to skip.
This mirrors what upstream setuptools did when dropping ImpImporter support.

Note: the sibling `import imp` fallback (line ~48) is already guarded by a
`try: import _imp` that succeeds on 3.13, and the two `import cgi` uses are
lazy imports on the PyPI upload/classifier-download paths only (never hit
during a wheel build), so no further changes are needed for the build path.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [langdale ships setuptools 65.0.2; a real fix
is a version bump to a py3.13-compatible setuptools]

--- a/pkg_resources/__init__.py
+++ b/pkg_resources/__init__.py
@@ -2188,7 +2188,10 @@ def resolve_egg_link(path):
     return next(dist_groups, ())


-register_finder(pkgutil.ImpImporter, find_on_path)
+if hasattr(pkgutil, 'ImpImporter'):
+    # pkgutil.ImpImporter was removed in Python 3.12; the FileFinder
+    # registration below covers the real import system on 3.3+.
+    register_finder(pkgutil.ImpImporter, find_on_path)

 if hasattr(importlib_machinery, 'FileFinder'):
     register_finder(importlib_machinery.FileFinder, find_on_path)
@@ -2345,7 +2348,8 @@ def file_ns_handler(importer, path_item, packageName, module):
         return subpath


-register_namespace_handler(pkgutil.ImpImporter, file_ns_handler)
+if hasattr(pkgutil, 'ImpImporter'):
+    register_namespace_handler(pkgutil.ImpImporter, file_ns_handler)
 register_namespace_handler(zipimport.zipimporter, file_ns_handler)

 if hasattr(importlib_machinery, 'FileFinder'):
